  "speechText": "For me, I learn a new language or stack by connecting it to problems I already know. That's because the tool may change, but many core problems stay the same. For example, when I learn Temporal, I map it to retries, checkpoints, state, and long-running workflows. The same way, I moved from backend work into OCR, retrieval, LLM, and GPU inference. So I still need to learn the new APIs. But I do not relearn the fundamentals, so I can adapt fairly quickly.",
